-- infra/e2e/seed/30-phase2-batch1-fixture.sql.tmpl
--
-- Phase 2 batch 1 (mig-infra) — data-point parity fixture for the three
-- page-pairs this batch covers: /users (LINE tab), /user-detail?id=N,
-- /dashboard?tab=executive|crm. Applied AFTER the tenant-template seed
-- (database/migration_2026-05-25_tenant_template.sql, already piped in by
-- infra/e2e/run.mjs's seedDatabase()/parity.mjs's equivalent) against the
-- SAME app/tenant DB — no USE statement of its own, same convention as
-- 20-admin-user.sql.tmpl (the caller prepends `USE \`<app-db>\`;`).
--
-- No __PLACEHOLDER__ substitution needed (nothing here is DB-name- or
-- secret-shaped) — the .sql.tmpl extension is kept only to match this
-- directory's established numbered-template naming convention, per this
-- batch's brief.
--
-- DETERMINISM: every timestamp below is a MySQL/MariaDB relative-date
-- expression (NOW() / CURDATE() / DATE_SUB(NOW(), INTERVAL n DAY|HOUR)),
-- never a hardcoded wall-clock literal — the harness's seed step and the
-- parity runner's PHP/Next fetches happen within the same short-lived
-- process run, so "today" at seed time and "today" at query time are always
-- the same calendar day. This mirrors the technique run.mjs/other seed
-- files use for the same reason (never assume a fixed date survives a
-- re-run on a different day). Buckets are spaced with a wide safety margin
-- (3d / 15d / 45d, not 6d / 29d / 31d) precisely so this holds even with
-- a slow docker build in between seed and query.
--
-- CURRENT-BOT-ID NOTE: @reya/auth's login() always sets a fresh tenant
-- session's currentBotId to null (packages/auth/src/session.ts), and
-- includes/header.php's own $currentBotId auto-select logic falls back to
-- null the same way when `line_accounts` has no rows (verified empirically
-- by infra/e2e/probe-page.md — this harness deliberately never seeds
-- line_accounts). Both sides are therefore ALWAYS null here. Every query in
-- users.php/queries.ts, crm.php/crmData.ts, AutoTagManager.php/crmData.ts
-- that filters with the literal-NULL-safe `(line_account_id = ? OR ? IS
-- NULL)` pattern (same placeholder bound both sides) is therefore always
-- unscoped — but the OTHER pattern, `x.line_account_id = ? OR
-- x.line_account_id IS NULL` (single placeholder, column-vs-NULL on the
-- right), only matches rows whose OWN line_account_id is NULL. That second
-- pattern is what user_tags/auto_tag_rules are read through (getAllTags(),
-- crm.php's tags-with-counts query, AutoTagManager::getRules()) — so every
-- `user_tags`/`auto_tag_rules` row below is seeded with `line_account_id =
-- NULL` on purpose. Getting this wrong would make tags/auto-rules silently
-- vanish from both stacks' dropdowns/counts identically, which would NOT
-- fail parity (both sides still agree) but WOULD make this fixture
-- pointless for those data points — a "trivially passing" bug, not a
-- crashing one, so called out explicitly here.

